Copyright (c) 2012- Matplotlib Development Team; All Rights Reserved.
License: matplotlib license (a PSF-style permissive license).
Upstream: https://github.com/matplotlib/matplotlib

vplot's rendering core is derived from matplotlib's C++ extension sources. The
derived files live under source/vplot/render/mpl/ and each carries a header
naming its matplotlib origin:

    _backend_agg.h, _backend_agg.cpp   Agg renderer driver
    _backend_agg_basic_types.h         GCAgg, ClipPath, Dashes, SketchParams
    path_converters.h                  path pipeline: NaN removal, clipping,
                                       snapping, simplification, sketch
    agg_workaround.h                   Agg pixel-format workarounds
    array.h                            scalar/empty array-likes
    mplutils.h                         shared helpers
    vpl_adaptors.h                     rewritten from src/py_adaptors.h

Modifications: the CPython and pybind11 coupling has been removed. Concretely,
src/py_adaptors.h (which adapted NumPy arrays to Agg's vertex-source interface)
was rewritten as vpl_adaptors.h over plain C arrays; the pybind11 type_casters
for e_snap_mode, ClipPath, Dashes, SketchParams and GCAgg were deleted; and
py::value_error was replaced with std::invalid_argument. The algorithms are
otherwise unmodified, which is deliberate -- output fidelity against
matplotlib is the point.

Colormap, named-colour and mathtext data tables transcribed from matplotlib's
Python sources are likewise derivative works of matplotlib.


